{"text": "Friday.\n\nOn Wednesday, Nia looked at the sky for ten minutes. On Thursday, she looked for half an hour. It was getting easier.\n\nLeo taught her about clouds.\n\n\"The small white ones are nice,\" he said. \"But they never bring rain. You need big grey ones. Dark and heavy, like old blankets.\"\n\nOn Friday morning, the sky was white and flat. Nia ran outside early.\n\nThen the clouds came. They got darker and bigger. Soon they were bigger than all the clouds in Nia's books.\n\nThe wind was cooler now. The trees moved.\n\n\"Here it comes,\" said Grandma Edda.\n\nEveryone waited.\n\nGrandma put buckets in the garden. Leo and Nia stood in the dry field. Nia turned her face up to the sky.\n\nThey waited for ten minutes. Then an hour. Then all afternoon.\n\nNothing fell. Not one drop.\n\nIn the evening, the wind changed. Slowly, the grey clouds moved away to the east. Behind them, the sky was clear and hot again.\n\n\"It happens,\" said Grandma Edda softly. \"The clouds were only passing.\"\n\nNia went inside without a word.\n\nIn her room, Nia sat on the bed.\n\nShe opened her notebook and wrote. Only five days are left. Then we are going to fly home.\n\nA tear fell on the page. Then another one.\n\nSomeone knocked on the door. It was Leo.\n\n\"Are you OK?\" he asked.\n\n\"I'm fine,\" said Nia. But her voice was not fine.\n\nLeo looked at her for a long time. Then he closed the door quietly.\n\nA minute later, Nia heard the back door. Then she heard nothing.\n\nLate at night, Nia woke up.\n\nThere was a sound on the roof. Tap. Tap, tap.\n\nShe sat up in bed. The sound got faster. Tap-tap-tap-tap. It was soft, and it was everywhere.\n\nNia's heart jumped. She knew this sound from old films.\n\nShe ran to the window. It was dark outside, but the glass was wet.\n\nNia ran down the stairs in her pyjamas. She opened the back door.\n\nEverything was wet.", "textSha256": "20c0347e3d694a4179c7cd79b183666cec57ba05c75549519f7dbdcde9ea8b0d", "voice_id": "EXAVITQu4vr4x